{"availability":"available","full":"jeweledtech/bare-metal-forth","name":"bare-metal-forth","description":"Boots into a Forth-83 environment on x86 hardware. No Linux, no Windows, no abstraction layers — just Forth running on the machine. The dictionary *is* the system. Load a different dictionary, you have a different system. There is no kernel/user split, no syscall boundary, no permission model","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":10,"forks":4,"created":"2026-02-08T04:34:54Z","updated":"2026-10-11T05:43:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://jeweledtech.github.io/bare-metal-forth/","topics":[],"demo":"https://jeweledtech.github.io/bare-metal-forth/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:17.984Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:17.984Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:17.984Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:17.984Z","stars":10,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["No Linux. No Windows. No HAL. No story. Just the machine.","ForthOS is a bare-metal Forth-83 operating system written from BIOS entry in x86 NASM and Forth. It boots in under a second on a USB stick, talks to your hardware directly, and gives you a REPL on the bare metal of a real computer — the way programmers worked before vendors decided you weren't allowed to anymore.","This repo contains the kernel and the free vocabulary set. Paid vocabulary packs (hardware drivers, binary translation tools, the metacompiler) live in a separate repository and are available at shop.jollygeniusinc.com."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jeweledtech/bare-metal-forth/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"07cd5a809d948900c0d5160d439a18dabb5d93857b4ec4825138325886a6b928","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.074Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.074Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"No Linux. No Windows. No HAL. No story. Just the machine.","sourceUrl":"htt